    37	**1** **INTRODUCTION**
    38	
    39	Mobile applications have become extremely popular, with currently over 5 million apps in the
    40	Google Play and Apple stores. To remain competitive in this thriving market and ensure a highquality user experience, app developers must swiftly address any issues reported by the users of
    41	their apps. When users experience a problem, they typically submit a bug report to describe the
    42	app failure and provide steps to reproduce the issue. After receiving such bug reports, developers
    43	need to first reproduce the failure following the provided steps [ 15 ] so that they can debug their
    44	app and fix the issue. However, the reproduction steps provided in these bug reports are often
    45	unclear, incomplete, or inaccurate [ 16, 31 ]. This can make it challenging for developers to reproduce
