  1056	**4.8** **Threats to Validity**
  1057	
  1058	4.8.1 External Validity. A potential threat to the external validity of our results is the representativeness of the selected bug reports. We have attempted to overcome this threat by searching
  1059	for subjects from the artifacts of five open-source datasets. It is worth noting that all the subjects
  1060	are real-world Android bug reports either from GitHub Issues [ 6 ] or Google Code [ 7 ]. Another
  1061	potential threat is the representativeness of the UTG used in our experiments. In the evaluation, we
  1062	tried our best to create the UTG as completely as possible using a dynamic crawler. However, there
  1063	could be a potential threat that these UTG may not be representative of the UTG used by real-world
  1064	developers in terms of completeness. With a more complete UTG, there might be additional event
  1065	paths that introduce noise into the search and prevent our approach from finding the correct event
  1066	path to reproduce the bug report. To better understand the potential implications of this threat,
  1067	we conducted a small-scale robustness study on the UTG . Specifically, we randomly selected ten
  1068	subjects that our approach successfully reproduced and manually enriched their UTG s to make
  1069	them as complete as possible. Then, we reran our approach using the new UTG s and found that
  1070	the reproduction results remained consistent with the original results.
  1071	
