  1073	4.8.2 Internal Validity. A potential threat to internal validity is the biases that could be introduced
  1074	when identifying the step entities. To mitigate this threat, the first two authors independently
  1075	conducted the same step entity identification process following the established practice from
  1076	the existing study [ 50 ]. Then, they compared their results and resolved the discrepancies via
  1077	discussion. Another threat is the potential biases that could influence the manual validation of the
  1078	UI events in Section 4.3. To address this threat, in the manual validation process, we referred to
  1079	the reproduction UI events information in the original dataset if provided. This information was
  1080	collected by the authors of the original dataset, which could help reduce bias.
