     1	# Environmental Requirements
     2	## Hardware Requirement
     3	The implementation has been tested on a physical x86 Linux machine (Ubuntu 20.04) with eight 3.6GHz CPUs and 32 GB of memory. Please also make sure your computer has at least 20 GB free disk space to run the experiments.
     4	
     5	## Software Requirement
     6	### Setup the environment with Docker (Recommended)
     7	The suggested way for setting up the running environment is to use the provided Docker container. As a prerequisite, you need to install `docker` and `docker-compose` on your computer. The implementation has been tested on `docker` 20.10.8 and `docker-compose` 1.29.2. Please refer to [official instruction](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) for installation. The related environment files (Docker files and python requirements) are in "BuildEnvironment" directory. 
     8	
     9	To start the docker container, execute the following command in the terminal.
    10	```bash
    11	# Estimated Time: 3m
    12	cd BuildEnvironment
    13	export ROOT_PROJECT=$(pwd)/../ && docker-compose run reproduction-gui-model bash
    14	```
    15	This command will build and start the docker container for Roam. Once the container is started, you will be at the bash interface inside the docker container. Please double check if the container is running successfully by executing `docker ps` in another terminal on your computer, which will list all the running docker containers. You should see two running containers "reproduction-gui-model" and "neo4j:5.16.0". Make sure to wait until the status of "neo4j:5.16.0" is "healthy" before proceeding to the next step.
    16	
    17	Once it's done, please follow the steps in "INSTALL.md" file to test out the running example.
    18	
    19	### Setup the environment without Docker
    20	You can also setup the running environment without Docker. Roam's running environment contains three components: Python environment, Android environment, and Neo4j Graph database.
    21	
    22	#### Setup Required System Library
    23	Roam requires a linux library `graphviz`, please run `apt-get install graphviz` to install it.
    24	
    25	
    26	#### Setup Python Environment
    27	Roam is experimented on Python 3.7. The python dependencies are declared in "./BuildEnvironment/requirements.txt" file. To install it, simply run `pip install -r requirements.txt` under the "BuildEnvironment" folder.
    28	
    29	Roam also needs a language model from Spacy. Please run `python -m spacy download en_core_web_lg` to download it.
    30	
    31	#### Setup Android Environment
    32	Roam depends on Android SDK to setup Android emulator and reproduce the bug reports on it. To setup the Android SDK, you can download the Android SDK tools following the [official instructions](https://developer.android.com/tools). Make sure you make the `adb` , `avdmanager` and `emulator` command available in the terminal (by adding their path to the PATH environment variable). Roam will need them to create and run the Android emulator.
    33	
    34	#### Setup Neo4j Environment
    35	Roam relies on Neo4j to access the pre-built UI transition graph. Here, we provide the easiest way to setup and start Neo4j using its official docker container.
    36	```bash
    37	cd BuildEnvironment
    38	export ROOT_PROJECT=$(pwd)/../ && docker-compose up neo4j
    39	```
    40	The above command will download the Neo4j docker container and start it for Roam to use. Before running Roam, please make sure the Neo4j container is running successfully by checking its status using the `docker ps` command. You should see the container "neo4j:5.16.0" and its status to be "healthy".
    41	
    42	Once you finished all above steps, you can run Roam in your terminal following the steps in "INSTALL.md".


